WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.432
A system retrieves candidates with BM

00:00:03.452 --> 00:00:06.074
twenty five, then scores that shortlist

00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:07.181
with a neural model.

00:00:07.357 --> 00:00:09.450
Two kinds of machinery appear in the

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.422
diagram. Does that make this hybrid

00:00:11.442 --> 00:00:14.734
retrieval? Pause and count the routes that

00:00:14.754 --> 00:00:16.730
actually supplied candidates.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.241
Under this chapter’s definition, it is

00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:24.154
multi stage with one candidate generation

00:00:24.174 --> 00:00:27.066
route. Hybrid combines candidates or

00:00:27.086 --> 00:00:29.682
scores from multiple retrieval routes.

00:00:30.586 --> 00:00:32.364
Why combine retrieval routes?

00:00:32.539 --> 00:00:34.349
Their blind spots can be partly

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:36.836
complementary. A lexical route may

00:00:36.856 --> 00:00:40.277
preserve an analysed rare identifier that

00:00:40.297 --> 00:00:42.596
a dense representation blurs.

00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:44.878
A dense route may bridge a paraphrase

00:00:44.898 --> 00:00:47.235
without a useful shared indexed term.

00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:50.155
Our identifier and wording examples are

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.951
illustrations, not model runs.

00:00:53.113 --> 00:00:56.031
Neither route is guaranteed to recover the

00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:57.448
intended evidence.

00:00:57.611 --> 00:00:59.756
Boolean conditions can add explicit

00:00:59.776 --> 00:01:02.410
control, and all routes remain sensitive

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.168
to their indexed text, analysis,

00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:07.281
representations and settings.

00:01:08.169 --> 00:01:09.654
The chapter gives a lexical list

00:01:09.674 --> 00:01:13.365
containing A, B, C, and a dense list

00:01:13.385 --> 00:01:15.645
containing C, A, D.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.565
A and C occur in both.

00:01:17.728 --> 00:01:20.530
B arrives only through the lexical list; D

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.449
only through the dense list.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.575
Merging those supplied identities gives

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:27.456
four distinct records.

00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:30.330
List only means outside the other supplied

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.147
list, not irrelevant.

00:01:32.309 --> 00:01:34.428
The system still needs a rule for turning

00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:37.018
the routes’ evidence into one order.

00:01:37.928 --> 00:01:40.524
Follow the first arrangement: BM twenty

00:01:40.544 --> 00:01:43.256
five retrieves a shortlist, a cross

00:01:43.276 --> 00:01:45.704
encoder reranks it, and the leading

00:01:45.724 --> 00:01:47.018
records are displayed.

00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:50.215
Candidate generation still came from one

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:50.897
route.

00:01:51.453 --> 00:01:53.607
This is a multi stage cascade.

00:01:53.769 --> 00:01:55.695
It is not hybrid under the book’s

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.202
operational definition.

00:01:57.377 --> 00:02:00.115
Vendor terminology varies; inspect which

00:02:00.135 --> 00:02:02.653
stages actually supplied records.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.419
Now consider one scoring stage that blends

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:08.919
lexical and dense candidate generation

00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:10.683
evidence into a ranking.

00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:13.094
It combines multiple retrieval routes

00:02:13.114 --> 00:02:15.658
without requiring a separate reranking

00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:18.261
cascade. That is the chapter’s example of

00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:21.018
hybrid without a multi stage arrangement.

00:02:21.566 --> 00:02:23.603
The distinction is about two different

00:02:23.623 --> 00:02:26.257
design questions: where candidate evidence

00:02:26.277 --> 00:02:28.628
comes from, and whether later operations

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:31.192
process an earlier stage’s output.

00:02:31.342 --> 00:02:33.577
A merged score still needs an explicit

00:02:33.597 --> 00:02:36.090
combination rule and appropriate treatment

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.197
of its inputs.

00:02:38.094 --> 00:02:41.126
A common combined arrangement runs lexical

00:02:41.146 --> 00:02:44.193
and dense retrieval, fuses their lists,

00:02:44.226 --> 00:02:46.010
then sends a shortlist to a richer

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.704
reranker. This has multiple candidate

00:02:48.724 --> 00:02:51.448
routes and later processing stages.

00:02:51.623 --> 00:02:53.793
It is both hybrid and multi stage.

00:02:54.364 --> 00:02:56.689
The additional route may admit useful

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.828
material missed by the other route.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.947
But the later reranker still inherits the

00:03:01.967 --> 00:03:04.124
merged candidate boundary.

00:03:04.274 --> 00:03:05.994
Neither it nor an answer writer can

00:03:06.014 --> 00:03:08.893
inspect a record omitted by every earlier

00:03:08.913 --> 00:03:11.650
route without another retrieval operation.

00:03:12.572 --> 00:03:15.664
A blend runs prescribed paths and combines

00:03:15.684 --> 00:03:16.656
what they return.

00:03:16.805 --> 00:03:19.698
Routing chooses which path or paths to run

00:03:19.718 --> 00:03:23.357
for this query: lexical, dense, or both.

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:26.038
If both supply lists, those lists still

00:03:26.058 --> 00:03:27.210
need to be combined.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:30.748
A one route run combines nothing under

00:03:30.768 --> 00:03:32.952
this definition, even if the product has

00:03:32.972 --> 00:03:35.026
several available retrievers.

00:03:35.201 --> 00:03:37.191
Routing may be controlled by a rule,

00:03:37.211 --> 00:03:38.853
classifier or model.

00:03:39.765 --> 00:03:42.426
For a concrete explanation, ask which

00:03:42.446 --> 00:03:44.861
candidate routes ran, what text each

00:03:44.881 --> 00:03:47.941
searched, how deep each supplied list was,

00:03:48.103 --> 00:03:50.569
how duplicate identities were reconciled,

00:03:50.732 --> 00:03:52.825
and what rule combined the evidence.

00:03:53.374 --> 00:03:55.436
Hybrid retrieval is not a quality

00:03:55.456 --> 00:03:57.498
guarantee. It depends on the evidence

00:03:57.518 --> 00:04:00.256
preserved, the allowed candidate depths

00:04:00.276 --> 00:04:01.685
and the combination rule.

00:04:01.848 --> 00:04:04.173
The next film follows four records through

00:04:04.193 --> 00:04:07.060
reciprocal rank fusion, a simple baseline

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.972
that uses positions instead of unlike raw

00:04:09.992 --> 00:04:10.886
scores.
